# ============================================================
# Project data / generated artifacts
# (large or regeneratable from the scripts next to them — not source code)
# Audited before the first real push to GitHub against its actual limits:
#   - hard block: any single file over 100MB (a normal `git push` rejects it outright)
#   - soft guidance: keep total repo size well under ~1GB for a healthy clone
# Everything NOT listed below IS tracked normally: all source code, all small CSVs
# (IAM/doctor splits, results, labels, cleaning/leakage reports), small config/
# tokenizer/checkpoint-metadata files, and CRNN's own checkpoints (~21MB each, under
# the limit, tracked on purpose).
# ============================================================

# --- Files over GitHub's 100MB hard limit — a normal `git push` will reject these.
#     Needs a separate transfer (Git LFS, cloud storage, manual copy, etc.).
#     Sizes (each ~1.27-2.54 GB): checkpoint/normal/trocr/model.safetensors;
#     checkpoint/doctor/trocr/baseline/checkpoint-{3954,4833}/{model.safetensors,optimizer.pt};
#     checkpoint/doctor/trocr_pilot/{baseline,clhaa}/final/model.safetensors ---
final_code/checkpoint/normal/trocr/model.safetensors
final_code/checkpoint/doctor/trocr/baseline/checkpoint-3954/model.safetensors
final_code/checkpoint/doctor/trocr/baseline/checkpoint-3954/optimizer.pt
final_code/checkpoint/doctor/trocr/baseline/checkpoint-4833/model.safetensors
final_code/checkpoint/doctor/trocr/baseline/checkpoint-4833/optimizer.pt
final_code/checkpoint/doctor/trocr_pilot/baseline/final/model.safetensors
final_code/checkpoint/doctor/trocr_pilot/clhaa/final/model.safetensors
# Safety net for the same pattern anywhere else under final_code/ (e.g. once TrOCR's
# full finetune finishes and produces checkpoint/doctor/trocr/clhaa/final/, or any
# future pipeline) — these two filenames are always huge for TrOCR, whichever
# pipeline/checkpoint they're under, so catch them unconditionally:
final_code/**/model.safetensors
final_code/**/optimizer.pt

# --- Raw/derived image folders. No single file here is anywhere near 100MB, but each
#     is thousands of individual files (2k-34k) - committing that many blows past the
#     soft repo-size guidance and makes clones slow. All regenerable from the scripts
#     documented in RUN_ORDER.md, given the right upstream data. Sizes: I_Am_Dataset/
#     ~1.6GB/34k+ files; doctor_raw/images/ ~58MB/10,347 files; doctor_clean/images/
#     ~57MB/10,050 files; preprocessed_doctor/ ~160MB/32,160 files;
#     preprocessed_doctor_test/ ~11MB/2,010 files ---
final_code/data/normal/I_Am_Dataset/
final_code/data/doctor/doctor_raw/images/
final_code/data/doctor/doctor_clean/images/
final_code/data/doctor/preprocessed_doctor/
final_code/data/doctor/preprocessed_doctor_test/

# --- combineDataset.py's 5 raw source folders, extracted directly into doctor_raw/
# (see combineDataset.py's SOURCE_FOLDERS) - not this project's own output, just the
# original downloads sitting alongside it, never meant to be committed ---
final_code/data/doctor/doctor_raw/Doctor Handwriting Recognition Dataset/
final_code/data/doctor/doctor_raw/RxHand Original/
final_code/data/doctor/doctor_raw/Doctor’s Handwritten Prescription BD dataset/

# --- previous_code/ (archived old/superseded/scope-excluded code and checkpoints,
# ~431 MB total, no single file over 50MB - technically pushable, but kept local-only
# on purpose so the pushed repo stays clean; see previous_code/README.md for why each
# item was archived rather than deleted) ---
previous_code/